<title>HONG KONG: South China Brokerage '96 net up sharply.</title>
<headline>South China Brokerage '96 net up sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   11.5   vs 2.6</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.0    vs 6.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    46.09  vs 10.27</p>
<p>    Turnover		     192.22 vs 158.79</p>
<p>    Company name		 South China Brokerage Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  May 14-16</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   May 23</p>
<p>NOTE - South China Brokerage is a financial services company.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one-for-one share prior to a share subdivision.</p>
<p>A subdivision of shares will be made on the basis that every issued and unissued share of the company of HK$0.10 will be subdivided into four subdivided shares.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nine H.K. cents (including interim dividend of three cents) vs 8.5 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
